@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home Page";
}

<!-- Landing Page Section -->
<!-- TODO Make background image full screen. Maybe take a picture of the trading setup and put a black overlay on it -->
<section id="landing-page" class="landing-section">
    <div class="container text-center text-white">
        <h1 class="display-4">Are you ready to level up your trading?</h1>
        <a href="#about" class="btn btn-primary">Let's go</a>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- About Section -->
<section id="about" class="p-5">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>About Us</h2>
        <p>
            Dobrusky Capital LLC, headquartered in Lincoln, Nebraska, is a day trading company founded in 2023 by Austin Dobrusky.
            Our primary focus is on trading derivative securities of the S&P 500, specifically options and futures contracts.
            Our approach is data-driven and grounded in understanding the fundamental dynamics of the market to make informed intraday trading decisions. We rely on our strengths in analyzing volume and price action data, coupled with market sentiment, to take calculated risks when opportunities present themselves.
            In addition to trading, Austin brings over 8 years of experience in software development. 
            We have applied this expertise to our trading strategies, developing three proprietary trading indicators that have become a cornerstone of our daily operations at Dobrusky Capital LLC.
        </p>
        <p>
            Beyond our trading activities, our mission is to provide as much value as possible to growing traders. 
            Understanding the difficulty of day trading, we are committed to sharing knowledge and resources to help others succeed in their trading journey. 
            This commitment is demonstrated through the free education we offer and the release of the "Dobrusky Capital LLC 90-Day Trading Journal," a tool designed to help traders continuously improve their trading skills and mindset.
            This meticulously structured trading journal, used daily at Dobrusky Capital LLC, has been instrumental in enhancing the company's consistency and performance.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>


<!-- Indicators Section -->
<section id="indicators" class="bg-light p-5">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Our Trading Indicators</h2>
        <p>
            We have developed three proprietary trading indicators for TradingView. These indicators are not designed to dictate when to enter or exit trades; rather, they provide fast and reliable information that may be missed otherwise. 
            This information can often make the difference between a winning and losing trade. You still need to know how to read the market; all that our indicators do is increase the speed at which you can read it.
            These indicators are stable and are currently undergoing testing in our daily trade operations at Dobrusky Capital LLC.
            They are not yet available for purchase but will be released as soon as the testing phase is complete.
        </p>


        <!-- Indicator 1 -->
        <div class="indicator-row">
            <img src="@Url.Content("~/images/volumeprofile.png")" alt="Volume Profile Indicator" class="indicator-image">
            <div class="indicator-description">
                <h3>Volume Profile</h3>
                <p>This indicator displays a volume profile (volume by price) that shows both cumulative volume and buy/sell pressure.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Indicator 2 -->
        <div class="indicator-row">
            <div class="indicator-description">
                <h3>Buy/Sell Volume Bars</h3>
                <p>This indicator displays buy/sell volume bars (volume by time). 
                    It features two customizable metrics to gauge a baseline volume. The indicator offers a simple moving average as well as a proprietary "baseline" metric.
                    The baseline during the regular market session will only be calculated using regular market session data and vice versa for extended hours. 
                    This method of calculation provides a more accurate baseline volume than the simple moving average.</p>
            </div>
            <img src="@Url.Content("~/images/volumebars.png")" alt="Buy/Sell Volume Bars Indicator" class="indicator-image">
        </div>

        <!-- Indicator 3 -->
        <div class="indicator-row">
            <img src="@Url.Content("~/images/vpaindicator.png")" alt="Volume Price Analysis Indicator" class="indicator-image">
            <div class="indicator-description">
                <h3>VPA Indicator</h3>
                <p>Inspired by the teachings in Anna Coulling's book "Volume Price Analysis", this indicator is designed to assist traders in identifying valuable volume price analysis (VPA) information on price charts. 
                    This indicator highlights important candlesticks, volume conditions, and price levels that can provide insights into potential market structure and direction.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Trading Journal Section -->
<section class="p-5">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Trading Journal</h2>
        <p>
            At Dobrusky Capital LLC we believe in the importance of journaling when trying to become a successful trader. 
            Without keeping track of each of your trades, the technical mistakes, and the psychological mistakes, you will never succeed, 
            and if you do manage to suceed without journaling, it will take you significantly longer than it would've otherwise. 
            We created this journal because we saw a need within the retail trading industry for a carefully structured journal 
            that will shorten the trading learning curve as much as possible. We created this journal first and foremost for the user of the company but we believe that any growing trader could find value within it.
        </p>
        <p>
            As mentioned above, our mission is to provide as much value to growing traders as we can. 
            We truly believe in the power of our journal, it has improved the performance of our company immensely, and we would like to share it with you.
            However we understand that a meticiously structured handwritten journal might not be for everyone, and we don't want to waste your time and money.
            The reason most traders fail is because they have no risk management rules. 
            They lose all of their money in a short period of time, preventing them from sticking around long enough to grow their skills enough to be consistent.
            We just want to see traders succeed so by subscribing to our email list not only grants you a free sneak peek at our invaluable journal but also provides access to a free education on risk management.
            Even if our journal isn't for you, we hope that through our free education on risk managment you can always live to trade another day and stay in the game for the long term success.
        </p>
        <p>
            The journal itself features detailed trade metrics, emotion tracking, and structured monthly, weekly, and quarterly reviews to
            support a comprehensive trading strategy. Its bonus sections, including performance tracking and SWOT analysis, further enrich 
            traders' approaches. By signing up, you gain insights into these tools that have significantly improved our consistency and 
            performance at Dobrusky Capital LLC.
        </p>
        <!-- Email Sign-Up Form -->
        <form>
            <div class="mb-3">
                <label for="emailInput" class="form-label">Email address</label>
                <input type="email" class="form-control" id="emailInput" placeholder="name@example.com">
            </div>
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Sign Up</button>
        </form>
    </div>
</section>
